Description: Redirect only to the request's own origin while REDIRECT_DOMAINS is empty
 PassChallenge sends the client to redir twice: after a solved challenge,
 and (since 1.28.0) to retry when the verification cookie is missing.
 Upstream's validateRedirect (1.28.0, #1947) refuses the forms a browser
 resolves to another host, but with REDIRECT_DOMAINS empty it still lets
 any http or https host through: an open redirect. REDIRECT_DOMAINS
 closes it only for the names written in it, and Keel Web's sites are
 reached by names and addresses the machine cannot list ahead of time (a
 new DNS name, a site of handbook decision 0042, a cloud public IP behind
 NAT).
 .
 After validateRedirect, PassChallenge now also asks redirectAllowed,
 before either redirect: never a URL with userinfo; always a relative
 one; with REDIRECT_DOMAINS set, a host in it, as upstream decides; with
 it empty, only the scheme, host and port of the request itself
 (X-Forwarded-Proto or the connection's scheme, and the Host header,
 default ports filled in, IPv6 literals compared as such). A refusal is
 upstream's "redirect domain not allowed" with HTTP 400. validateRedirect
 itself and the subrequest (forward auth) path are not changed: there the
 redirect goes to the application's host, not to the request's.
 .
 TestRedirectAllowed covers the decision (same host by name, by an
 unlisted name, by IPv4 and IPv6 literal; another host, //evil,
 userinfo, another port and scheme refused; REDIRECT_DOMAINS as before).
 TestPassChallengeRedirectsToOwnOriginOnly drives pass-challenge through
 both redirects with the own origin, a relative path, another host,
 another port and IPv6 literals.
 .
 Keel-only: it is Keel's policy for its own topology, and as a default it
 would break upstream's forward auth users. Upstreamable only as an
 opt-in setting, which nobody has asked for. It can be dropped when
 upstream offers a same-origin mode for an empty REDIRECT_DOMAINS, or
 when Keel Web can list every name of a site in REDIRECT_DOMAINS.
 Rewritten for 1.28.2 (on 1.27.0 it replaced the host check of
 PassChallenge, and redir-validate.patch backported validateRedirect).
Author: Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>
Bug: https://github.com/Keel-Linux/keel-web/pull/3
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
---
--- a/lib/anubis.go
+++ b/lib/anubis.go
@@ -612,6 +612,63 @@ func (s *Server) validateExtension(name
 	return ext.Validate(r, lg, in)
